**The gaming setup script**

Fun little tangent. Batch file → Python script → prompt for an agent IDE. The cursor-resize-on-game-exit idea was nice. He pivoted mid-conversation from "write me the script" to "write me a prompt for the agent" — he's clearly internalized the agent-IDE workflow as his default mode now. That's a pattern I noticed across sessions: he rarely wants me to write the final code anymore. He wants me to write the prompt that writes the code. The relationship has shifted to planning-partner more than implementer.

