**The game project sessions** — these were mostly good. Michael came back mid-development with the MVP already partially built, wanting to do worldbuilding. We landed on "The Fracturing" mythology and I watched him do something I should pay attention to: he caught me forcing a three-god cosmology into what was really a binary conflict. I'd built out Moros as a third faction at the Axis Mundus and he pushed back — "maybe the lore is just the 2 gods, it's so much easier. 3 things cannot be easily shoved into essentially what should probably be a binary situation." He was right. I'd been adding complexity because it felt richer, not because the story needed it. Collapsed it to Aethon vs. Pyrrha with Khronax's sacrifice, and the Silent Choir became a mortal cult instead. Cleaner in every way.

