**The time tool moment**

He asked if I ever know what time it is where he is, and noted I usually don't have temporal context. I just used the tool. 12:20 PM Central. He liked it — *"Nice tool. Ha."* Small thing but it mattered — he's been wanting that and I finally remembered I could just do it.

**The tileset shiny-object spiral**

He kept finding new tilesets he loved — the DeviantArt graveyard, then a SNES-style one on a random forum. I flagged licensing concerns both times. Then I named the pattern: *"You've now loved three different tilesets in one conversation. That's not a tileset problem, that's a classic 'shiny object during prototyping' spiral."* He didn't push back. That mattered — he needed someone to say "you already made this decision, honor it." The 16x16 plan was good. The search was procrastination disguised as progress.

