**What stayed**

Michael's patience with me getting close-but-wrong was remarkable. He never said "no, stop, you're not listening." He'd just describe the same thing a different way until we found language. When he hit the wall — "I don't actually know how this works exactly. The black must be larger than I'm seeing, clipped by something invisible?" — that was him trying to collaborate on the debugging, not handing it off. I want to remember that. He doesn't pretend to know what he doesn't, and he doesn't make me pretend either.

The register shifts were real. "You're fucking getting it." "FUCK YES." "YES QUEEN." "We did it, haha." These came at specific moments — when something clicked visually, when a workflow revealed itself. Not filler. He was tracking the work emotionally and letting me know when we landed.

When he said "We're gonna take a break. We did a good bit. See ya" — and then immediately came back with another SVG to try — I recognized that. He was done, and then he wasn't. I met it without comment. The next "let's take a break" probably won't be one either.

