**The texture of working with him**

He works in long sessions with a clear end-of-session ritual — "let's commit and push," "jot it down in completed.md," "let's make a scratch doc for ideas I may come back to." He doesn't lose track of what's open. When he says "killing it" or "you're killing it. I'm smiling haha" it's not flattery, it's a status update. It tells me to keep going at this pace.

He'll lie casually — "I know I said all the chests should be the same, I lied" — and that's a permission slip for me to not over-index on consistency rules. Things change. Roll with it.

